
# Fleet Telemetry Analytics

## Project Overview

An end-to-end fleet telemetry analytics project that uses Python and DuckDB to generate, process, and analyse synthetic IoT telemetry data across 50 vehicles.

The project processes **150,000 telemetry records**, applying data quality checks and star-schema modelling to transform raw telemetry data into structured datasets for fleet performance analytics.

## Technology Stack

- **Python:** Synthetic data generation and ETL processing.
- **DuckDB:** Database creation, data storage, and SQL transformations.
- **SQL:** Data processing and analytical queries.
- **Data Modelling:** Star-schema modelling.

## Project Structure

```text
Fleet_Telemetry_Analytics/
│
├── Data/
│   └── raw_telematry.csv
│
├── Data_Model/
│   └── Fleet_Operations_Data_Model.png
│
└── ETL_Python_Scripts/
    ├── Create_Database_and_Load_Raw_Fleet_Telemetry.ipynb
    └── Generate_Synthetic_Fleet_Telemetry_Data.ipynb
```

## Key Features

- Generated synthetic IoT telemetry data for 50 vehicles.
- Processed 150,000 telemetry records.
- Built a DuckDB database to store and manage fleet telemetry data.
- Implemented ETL workflows using Python and SQL.
- Applied data quality checks to improve data consistency.
- Designed a star-schema data model for fleet performance analytics.

## Project Objectives

The project demonstrates practical data engineering skills, including synthetic data generation, ETL development, database management, data quality validation, and dimensional data modelling.

